+---
+title: "bun/floating-effect"
+description: "Report Effect v4 values discarded by expression statements"
+# Generated by src/codegen/lint-rule-docs.ts. Do not edit below this line.
+plugin: "bun"
+aliases: []
+kind: "problem"
+category: null
+default: "off"
+fixable: "no"
+typeAware: true
+deprecated: false
+---
+
+Creating an Effect describes work. If a statement discards the Effect, the runtime never performs that work. Yield it inside an Effect generator, keep it for composition, or run it at the boundary of your program.
+
+{/* Generated by src/codegen/lint-rule-docs.ts. Do not edit this section. */}
+
+## Configure
+
+Off by default. This rule needs types, so turning it on makes `bun lint` type check your code first.
+
+```toml bunfig.toml
+[lint.rules]
+"bun/floating-effect" = "error" # or "warn"
+```
+
+{/* End of the generated section. */}
+
+Bun also reads the `@effect/language-service` plugin in the project's `tsconfig.json`. Set `diagnosticSeverity.floatingEffect` to `"error"`, `"warning"`, or `"off"`. A setting in the lint config takes precedence. Projects using an oxlint configuration need type-aware linting enabled.
+
+## Examples
+
+{/* bad {"packages": {"effect": "4.1.4"}} */}
+
+```ts
+import { Effect } from "effect";
+
+Effect.log("forgotten");
+```
+
+{/* good {"packages": {"effect": "4.1.4"}} */}
+
+```ts
+import { Effect } from "effect";
+
+export const notify = Effect.gen(function* () {
+  yield* Effect.log("ready");
+});
+```
